WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
This is the Virtual Patient Clinic, a simulator for medical students.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:12.080
They can interview AI patients by voice, do examinations, order tests and make diagnoses,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.160
then get feedback tied to what was actually said and done.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:23.160
Here's a short visit with Linda Hale.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.840
Hi Ms. Hale, I'm one of the medical students.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.080
What brings you in today?

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.320
I've had this burning pain right here in my upper stomach for a few weeks, and honestly

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.200
I'm exhausted all the time.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.960
It's been really wearing me down, especially with work.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.760
I'm sorry that sounds miserable, when did it start?

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:46.760
Thank you.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.480
It started about a month ago, and it's definitely gotten worse over the last couple of weeks.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.560
Are you taking anything for it, any over-the-counter pain relievers?

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:03.680
Yeah, I've been taking Tums, and they help for maybe an hour, then it kind of comes right

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:09.400
back, and I take ibuprofen pretty much every day for my back usually two or three at a time.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.040
Have you noticed any change in your bowel movements?

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.800
Are your stools darker or black?

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:21.800
Yeah, actually, now that you mention it, they've been darker than usual the last few

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.880
days, almost black.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:29.000
That's part of why I finally decided I shouldn't ignore this.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Thank you.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.000
That's really important.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:38.000
You mentioned you're exhausted. How have things been for you lately, outside of this?

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.680
It's been a lot.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.120
Honestly, I got divorced about eight months ago, and I'm juggling work real estate hours

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.160
are all over the place, and my two teenagers are with me about half the week.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.880
I'm just running on fumes, and my sleep is terrible.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:54.280
That's a lot to carry.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:58.320
Many people under that kind of stress find they're drinking more than usual.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.480
Have you been drinking alcohol these days?

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:06.880
Yeah, I mean, I'll have a glass of wine with dinner sometimes.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:07.880
Pretty normal.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.120
I'm more worried about what's going on with my stomach though.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.640
All right, no judgment at all.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:17.160
On a typical night, honestly, how much is it?

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:24.160
Okay, since the divorce, it's been more like a bottle of wine, most nights, sometimes more

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.080
if it's been a really rough day.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.080
I know it's too much.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.920
I'm not proud of it.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:34.160
I really appreciate you telling me, let's do a physical exam and look at your stomach

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.160
and abdomen.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.960
Okay, I'm fine with that.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.680
Whatever you need to do, I just really want to figure out why this burning is happening

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.600
and get some relief.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:53.600
Then the student can order an abdominal physical exam, say a CBC and maybe liver function tests.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:03:01.120
When they return to the transcript, they'll see the results of those tests.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:11.200
And then they can wrap things up in the encounter.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:18.360
And then go ahead and enter their diagnosis.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:27.230
After they've entered that, they click and the language model goes through and examines

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:34.230
the transcript, examines the diagnosis and looks at it and grades it based on a basic

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:41.810
rubric that the doctor or professor has entered and gives them some feedback.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:49.750
You can see that this sees little things about what to work on and what they did and what

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.750
they didn't do and how they did on communicating and things like that.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.190
And then they have their full transcript available.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.510
That's the virtual patient clinic.
